WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.300
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.400 --> 00:01.550
Podduang.

3
00:01.550 --> 00:04.530
Do you also think that Anda was murdered?

4
00:04.530 --> 00:06.844
Yeah, I think so, too.

5
00:06.844 --> 00:07.900
Itti,

6
00:07.900 --> 00:11.420
I promise you, if someone's behind this,

7
00:11.420 --> 00:13.320
they're going to jail.

8
00:13.320 --> 00:15.006
Thank you very much, Lieutenant.

9
00:15.900 --> 00:17.640
And you just bought a new one?

10
00:17.640 --> 00:20.500
I bought a new one to replace it. It didn't cost much.

11
00:20.500 --> 00:24.360
The box might be slightly damaged. It was probably a QC reject.

12
00:25.230 --> 00:26.400
Dunk, you asshole.

13
00:26.400 --> 00:28.280
I won't let you borrow my things ever again.

14
00:28.280 --> 00:29.530
Help me.

15
00:29.530 --> 00:30.930
Help.

16
00:30.930 --> 00:32.440
Then would you believe me...

17
00:32.440 --> 00:35.488
If I told you that I've heard those voices for as long as I can remember?

18
00:35.488 --> 00:36.844
Jinna. Jinna.

19
00:36.844 --> 00:38.180
Jinna, Jinna, help me.

20
00:38.180 --> 00:39.350
Hello?

21
00:39.350 --> 00:41.700
Hello? Hey, hello?

22
00:41.700 --> 00:42.800
Help me.

23
00:42.800 --> 00:44.473
Help me.

24
00:57.750 --> 00:59.644
I'm sorry. Are you okay?

25
01:04.160 --> 01:05.330
Watch where you're going!

26
01:05.330 --> 01:08.355
You were too busy looking at your phone, too. That's why...

27
01:14.200 --> 01:16.790
How am I supposed to get through the day like this?

28
01:38.530 --> 01:39.844
Does it fit?

29
01:39.844 --> 01:42.590
I didn't know which one to pick.

30
01:42.590 --> 01:44.844
Well, it does fit,

31
01:44.844 --> 01:48.210
but I haven't worn a pleated skirt since I was a freshman.

32
01:48.210 --> 01:52.155
Wearing a long one makes me look like a dork.

33
01:55.230 --> 01:59.120
You look cute in it, though.

34
01:59.120 --> 02:00.960
Don't you think so?

35
02:02.640 --> 02:06.880
Weren't you embarrassed having to buy a skirt?

36
02:06.880 --> 02:09.794
If I were, who would have bought it for you?

37
02:12.480 --> 02:16.993
Yeah. So where are you heading now?

38
02:18.760 --> 02:21.244
I'm going to the soccer club.

39
02:21.244 --> 02:23.780
That's perfect. I'll come with you.

40
02:25.844 --> 02:27.450
Okay.

41
02:32.360 --> 02:33.640
Put some energy into it.

42
02:33.640 --> 02:35.390
Be more agile.

43
02:35.390 --> 02:37.010
Don't step on the lines.

44
02:37.010 --> 02:38.950
Good. Nice.

45
02:41.020 --> 02:42.488
Go.

46
02:43.888 --> 02:45.970
Keep going.

47
03:21.490 --> 03:24.577
What are you doing? Are you going to sit down?

48
03:34.690 --> 03:38.513
So, is Jinna really flirting with you?

49
03:40.488 --> 03:43.290
Well, something like that.

50
03:43.290 --> 03:44.930
How is that possible?

51
03:44.930 --> 03:46.420
You're...

52
03:48.210 --> 03:50.393
not even his type.

53
03:52.311 --> 03:55.620
By the way, do you like him?

54
03:59.610 --> 04:00.933
Why do you ask?

55
04:00.933 --> 04:04.970
Well, I just want to know. Do you like him?

56
04:09.888 --> 04:12.859
I don't know. We've only just started talking.

57
04:25.533 --> 04:27.680
Then I'm going to go after Jinna.

58
04:33.360 --> 04:35.400
Suit yourself.

59
04:53.450 --> 04:56.620
[Characters, places, and incidents in this production]

60
04:56.620 --> 04:58.311
[are entirely fictitious.]

61
04:58.311 --> 05:01.120
[Viewer discretion is advised.]

62
06:20.110 --> 06:22.126
He's the one who killed Anda.

63
06:23.250 --> 06:25.406
Just confess already.

64
06:25.406 --> 06:26.830
- Tell everyone you killed him! - Stop it.

65
06:26.830 --> 06:28.040
That's enough.

66
06:28.040 --> 06:29.960
This is going too far.

67
06:29.960 --> 06:31.680
My parents are sitting right there.

68
06:31.680 --> 06:34.250
At the very least, show them some respect.

69
06:39.640 --> 06:43.840
Do you really think that Anda killed himself?

70
06:45.230 --> 06:47.511
What I think is none of your business.

71
06:47.511 --> 06:52.740
All you care about is losing your job because my brother died.

72
06:52.740 --> 06:54.530
Go throw your tantrum somewhere else.

73
06:54.530 --> 06:57.244
Don't do it at my brother's funeral.

74
06:57.244 --> 07:00.955
You... ruined my life.

75
07:00.955 --> 07:03.711
- You bastard! - Go.

76
07:03.711 --> 07:04.760
Leave.

77
07:15.244 --> 07:20.533
As for you, I don't see any need for you to be here.

78
07:22.920 --> 07:26.046
Kum was Anda's boyfriend, after all.

79
07:26.840 --> 07:30.040
I don't think it's unusual for him to be at Anda's funeral.

80
07:30.040 --> 07:33.766
That's right. I think he has every reason to be here.

81
07:45.444 --> 07:47.022
Come on, Mom.

82
07:50.080 --> 07:51.800
Are you okay?

83
07:51.800 --> 07:53.880
I am.

84
07:53.880 --> 07:55.293
Thanks.

85
08:08.160 --> 08:11.880
I know you're sad, but you should eat something.

86
08:11.880 --> 08:14.050
Here, it's still warm.

87
08:17.000 --> 08:20.240
Yeah, you need to eat.

88
08:20.240 --> 08:22.240
You've lost so much weight.

89
08:27.286 --> 08:29.960
You know what makes you look suspicious?

90
08:29.960 --> 08:32.500
The way you're acting right now.

91
08:32.500 --> 08:36.760
I know you're grieving and can't process it yet,

92
08:36.760 --> 08:39.699
but you have to prove your innocence, too.

93
08:42.520 --> 08:45.440
Sorry, can I ask you something?

94
08:46.773 --> 08:51.240
Why did you say you were the reason Anda died?

95
08:51.240 --> 08:57.560
I know you didn't mean you killed him,

96
08:57.560 --> 08:59.039
but I want to know...

97
08:59.920 --> 09:05.088
if it has anything to do with you breaking up with him.

98
09:05.088 --> 09:07.720
- You're... - I'm Podduang.

99
09:07.720 --> 09:11.880
Let's just say I'm a friend of Anda's friend.

100
09:18.770 --> 09:20.060
It does.

101
09:21.800 --> 09:26.593
That breakup message was actually from me.

102
09:28.520 --> 09:33.010
But if I'd known that he was facing something much worse,

103
09:34.360 --> 09:39.511
the pressure I was under would have meant nothing.

104
09:44.800 --> 09:46.911
Who was putting pressure on you?

105
09:50.720 --> 09:52.320
Well...

106
09:53.520 --> 09:55.080
That day...

107
09:55.844 --> 09:58.000
Can't you answer that?

108
09:58.000 --> 10:03.880
I asked how much longer you planned to stay together.

109
10:11.088 --> 10:12.755
No answer?

110
10:12.755 --> 10:19.030
Then I guess that means you can't see it either, right?

111
10:19.030 --> 10:25.111
You can't see how long the love between two men will last.

112
10:33.760 --> 10:36.640
Sir, well...

113
10:38.100 --> 10:41.700
I know it might seem strange to you,

114
10:43.400 --> 10:45.339
but I intend to love

115
10:46.730 --> 10:48.970
and take care of Anda

116
10:50.210 --> 10:51.986
for as long as possible.

117
10:52.910 --> 10:55.800
Just like any other couple.

118
10:55.800 --> 10:57.760
Aren't you ashamed of what people think?

119
10:57.760 --> 10:59.819
Two men living together?

120
11:04.380 --> 11:05.822
I...

121
11:07.113 --> 11:08.726
I'm not ashamed.

122
11:12.500 --> 11:16.888
Do you think Anda will be ashamed, though?

123
11:20.353 --> 11:22.586
My son is still young.

124
11:23.226 --> 11:24.833
He's still naive.

125
11:27.139 --> 11:30.520
What if one day he comes to his senses

126
11:30.520 --> 11:35.619
and looks back on this, only to realize he was wrong?

127
11:35.619 --> 11:37.330
Won't he be ashamed?

128
11:38.646 --> 11:42.540
Look. Anda is famous.

129
11:42.540 --> 11:45.240
His family comes from an old, refined background.

130
11:47.093 --> 11:50.244
He's not just anyone who can do whatever he wants.

131
11:50.244 --> 11:51.826
Do you realize that?

132
12:06.040 --> 12:07.746
I'm begging you.

133
12:10.120 --> 12:12.480
Can you let him go for now?

134
12:20.286 --> 12:21.806
At the very least,

135
12:23.340 --> 12:25.920
let him grow up first.

136
12:25.920 --> 12:27.946
Let him become more mature,

137
12:30.810 --> 12:33.553
learn more about the world,

138
12:34.453 --> 12:41.140
and experience the adult world for himself before he makes up his mind.

139
12:44.800 --> 12:50.426
And when that day comes, if he still insists on being with you,

140
12:51.060 --> 12:53.806
I will give it another thought.

141
12:57.760 --> 12:59.193
However,

142
13:00.520 --> 13:01.920
for now,

143
13:04.550 --> 13:06.860
I'm asking you to help Anda.

144
13:07.720 --> 13:11.800
It hurts both me and my wife

145
13:11.800 --> 13:17.320
every time we see our own son being attacked by people online.

146
13:20.580 --> 13:22.980
I raised him well.

147
13:35.050 --> 13:37.119
Don't ruin his life.

148
14:13.240 --> 14:14.493
So...

149
14:16.360 --> 14:19.546
you texted Anda to break up with him?

150
14:22.840 --> 14:24.119
Yes.

151
14:27.166 --> 14:29.180
Right then and there.

152
14:29.180 --> 14:30.733
I let his dad see it.

153
14:33.000 --> 14:36.940
That means you were at Anda's the whole time?

154
14:36.940 --> 14:38.730
That's right.

155
14:38.730 --> 14:41.330
I told you I didn't kill him.

156
14:42.940 --> 14:45.410
How could I hurt the person I love most?

157
14:49.688 --> 14:54.050
Then who do you think killed him?

158
14:54.050 --> 14:55.990
I'll be honest with you, Jinna.

159
14:58.570 --> 15:01.906
If you ever went through something like this...

160
15:04.170 --> 15:08.240
If the person you loved most was suddenly taken from you,

161
15:11.240 --> 15:13.413
you wouldn't care about anything.

162
15:14.360 --> 15:18.290
The culprit, the cause of death, or anything else.

163
15:19.320 --> 15:21.360
All you'd think about...

164
15:23.090 --> 15:25.400
is a life without them.

165
15:26.000 --> 15:31.546
You'd just feel like your world had already fallen apart.

166
15:33.440 --> 15:37.240
Who the culprit is or who did it,

167
15:39.153 --> 15:40.800
I don't know.

168
15:43.906 --> 15:45.710
I'm sorry.

169
15:46.400 --> 15:50.800
I was so focused on the culprit that I forgot what you were going through.

170
15:55.020 --> 15:56.686
It's okay.

171
15:56.686 --> 15:58.100
I understand.

172
15:59.873 --> 16:04.933
Anyway, I have to thank you all for trying so hard for Anda.

173
16:08.699 --> 16:12.900
If there's anything I can do to help, just let me know.

174
16:12.900 --> 16:15.000
I'm more than happy to do my best.

175
16:16.650 --> 16:18.413
I also want to know

176
16:19.820 --> 16:23.673
who was cruel enough to do this to Anda.

177
16:31.780 --> 16:34.565
All right, let's eat.

178
16:34.565 --> 16:36.320
Let's stop stressing out.

179
16:36.320 --> 16:37.700
Come on.

180
16:37.700 --> 16:40.533
Come on, have some food.

181
16:42.970 --> 16:44.710
Do you want anything?

182
16:44.710 --> 16:46.840
This is fine. The rice porridge.

183
16:48.840 --> 16:50.246
Go ahead.

184
17:06.130 --> 17:09.050
It wasn't Itti, the last person to be with him.

185
17:11.570 --> 17:14.820
And it wasn't Kum the one who broke up with him.

186
17:18.505 --> 17:20.622
Then who did this to you, Anda?

187
17:20.622 --> 17:22.422
Who was it?

188
17:46.450 --> 17:47.810
What the hell are you looking at?

189
17:47.810 --> 17:50.930
You're still doing okay?

190
17:50.930 --> 17:53.240
I heard you screaming last night.

191
17:54.240 --> 17:56.240
I'm fine.

192
17:56.240 --> 17:58.080
Where are you going?

193
17:59.260 --> 18:00.644
I'm going swimming.

194
18:00.644 --> 18:04.090
Do you want to come? It might help relieve your stress.

195
18:04.090 --> 18:06.840
Or just stay and keep screaming into your pillow.

196
18:07.800 --> 18:09.240
Fine.

197
18:09.960 --> 18:11.440
Let's go.

198
18:16.400 --> 18:19.640
What's gotten into you, going swimming at this hour?

199
18:19.640 --> 18:23.170
This is the best time to get the adrenaline pumping

200
18:23.170 --> 18:25.222
so I can stay active all day.

201
18:25.950 --> 18:29.010
Your life must be nice. You don't have anything to worry about.

202
18:33.900 --> 18:35.400
Podduang!

203
18:51.800 --> 18:53.160
Podduang!

204
19:41.530 --> 19:43.130
What are you looking at?

205
19:45.286 --> 19:47.110
You're in really good shape.

206
19:48.670 --> 19:50.580
Well, I'm an athlete.

207
19:50.580 --> 19:52.866
How could I not be in shape?

208
19:52.866 --> 19:56.844
You should exercise more yourself, since you're just that tiny.

209
19:59.050 --> 20:02.306
I'm what they call compact.

210
20:06.640 --> 20:09.960
Are you really a swimming instructor?

211
20:11.206 --> 20:14.600
Yeah, why would I lie?

212
20:15.790 --> 20:19.093
I teach elementary kids. Just private lessons.

213
20:19.093 --> 20:21.090
So I have to come here to teach them.

214
20:21.090 --> 20:23.120
They live in the same place you do.

215
20:26.380 --> 20:28.140
You sure do so many things.

216
20:47.622 --> 20:49.033
What are you thinking about?

217
20:51.820 --> 20:53.246
About Anda.

218
20:56.220 --> 20:58.373
I don't know how to help him.

219
21:00.340 --> 21:02.140
The police are so slow.

220
21:02.140 --> 21:03.473
They're useless.

221
21:05.533 --> 21:07.333
Did you bring your earbuds?

222
21:14.680 --> 21:17.830
I tried to listen this morning, but I couldn't hear anything.

223
21:25.120 --> 21:28.100
Can I keep them for now?

224
21:28.100 --> 21:29.540
What for?

225
21:30.173 --> 21:31.760
Well.

226
21:31.760 --> 21:35.120
Didn't you say you didn't hear anything?

227
21:36.080 --> 21:37.900
So why keep them?

228
21:37.900 --> 21:40.186
You can use mine for now.

229
21:40.186 --> 21:43.300
Man, just take them, then.

230
21:44.113 --> 21:45.646
I'll just buy new ones.

231
21:46.493 --> 21:48.506
I don't like using things someone else used.

232
21:49.620 --> 21:51.320
So I'm someone else now?

233
21:52.940 --> 21:54.466
Yeah, just take them.

234
21:54.466 --> 21:56.300
I'll find something for myself.

235
22:05.280 --> 22:09.000
But I got these earbuds from Dunk.

236
22:13.386 --> 22:15.393
Where did he buy them?

237
22:24.820 --> 22:27.940
You called me over just to ask where I bought these earbuds?

238
22:27.940 --> 22:30.600
Why didn't you just call? I'm busy.

239
22:30.600 --> 22:33.960
Busy with what? You were playing games loudly, trying to make my ears bleed.

240
22:36.177 --> 22:40.220
Dunk, where did you get these earbuds?

241
22:40.220 --> 22:42.420
I bought them from an online shop.

242
22:42.420 --> 22:43.680
My regular page.

243
22:43.680 --> 22:45.740
They sell literally everything.

244
22:45.740 --> 22:47.866
Which page? Let me see.

245
22:49.044 --> 22:50.440
Is it this one?

246
22:50.440 --> 22:52.110
We've got stuff from everywhere today.

247
22:52.110 --> 22:53.370
We have everything.

248
22:53.370 --> 22:55.280
Everything you'd ever want, guys.

249
22:55.280 --> 22:57.440
Yeah, they're live right now.

250
22:58.673 --> 22:59.680
I knew it.

251
22:59.680 --> 23:02.986
This page sells either fakes or knock-offs.

252
23:02.986 --> 23:06.080
Wait, they told me they were QC rejects.

253
23:06.080 --> 23:07.640
Let me see.

254
23:09.420 --> 23:12.820
Various shirts in various styles.

255
23:12.820 --> 23:15.630
What's our special item today?

256
23:15.630 --> 23:17.240
We've got jackets today.

257
23:19.150 --> 23:20.460
Cool?

258
23:20.460 --> 23:23.000
- Is something wrong? - So many of them.

259
23:23.000 --> 23:25.600
- The jacket the vendor is wearing... - They're all high quality.

260
23:25.600 --> 23:26.846
Why?

261
23:28.340 --> 23:32.300
- I bought the jacket for Anda. - Get it at a low price!

262
23:38.313 --> 23:40.520
I'm sure it's the same one.

263
23:42.760 --> 23:43.900
Boots? Okay.

264
23:43.900 --> 23:45.244
Got it.

265
23:53.560 --> 23:54.900
Are you serious?

266
23:54.900 --> 23:58.360
I have no idea where they get their stock.

267
23:58.360 --> 24:01.566
Do you think they'll tell you where they got the earbuds?

268
24:02.361 --> 24:03.926
They'll have to.

269
24:07.766 --> 24:09.020
Art?

270
24:09.020 --> 24:10.370
Hello, Art.

271
24:10.370 --> 24:12.640
A regular customer!

272
24:12.640 --> 24:15.713
You're picking up the shirt yourself today?

273
24:15.713 --> 24:17.640
- Are you in a hurry to use it? - Yes.

274
24:17.640 --> 24:21.133
By the way, there's another one I actually want.

275
24:21.133 --> 24:24.880
I saw you wearing it in the livestream. This one.

276
24:24.880 --> 24:28.620
Right. I was just wearing it in the livestream.

277
24:28.620 --> 24:32.260
Cute, isn't it? But it belongs to my friend. It's not for sale.

278
24:32.260 --> 24:35.520
Why? Why is it not for sale?

279
24:35.520 --> 24:37.660
How much do you want?

280
24:37.660 --> 24:40.620
It's not about the price. It's just not mine to sell.

281
24:40.620 --> 24:44.288
There are plenty of other clothes. Lots of cool items. Take your pick.

282
24:46.260 --> 24:47.710
It really is Anda's.

283
24:47.710 --> 24:49.780
[AD] I had this embroidered here.

284
24:50.880 --> 24:53.066
This one really isn't for sale.

285
24:56.040 --> 24:58.160
Take me to your friend.

286
24:58.160 --> 25:00.800
Please calm down. Calm down, okay?

287
25:00.800 --> 25:02.560
Li.

288
25:02.560 --> 25:04.940
What is it now?

289
25:04.940 --> 25:07.820
You're bringing me a guy?

290
25:07.820 --> 25:09.879
Yeah, they're here to see you.

291
25:11.200 --> 25:12.813
Where did you get this jacket?

292
25:15.740 --> 25:18.250
I... don't remember.

293
25:18.250 --> 25:19.986
I don't know. I can't remember.

294
25:21.000 --> 25:23.073
I asked where you got this jacket.

295
25:25.680 --> 25:27.490
Maybe it's my dad's.

296
25:27.490 --> 25:29.060
I don't know where he bought it.

297
25:29.060 --> 25:30.840
I thought it looked nice, so I just grabbed it.

298
25:30.840 --> 25:34.806
Call your dad and ask him where he got this jacket.

299
25:42.960 --> 25:44.660
Hello?

300
25:44.660 --> 25:46.300
Hello, Dad.

301
25:46.300 --> 25:50.250
Where did you get this new jacket?

302
25:50.250 --> 25:51.540
Which one?

303
25:51.540 --> 25:54.830
The denim jacket with the leather collar.

304
25:57.690 --> 26:01.240
I got it somewhere near my workplace.

305
26:01.240 --> 26:04.280
Are you sure you didn't take it from anyone?

306
26:04.280 --> 26:06.050
Yeah, why are you asking?

307
26:06.050 --> 26:08.510
I wouldn't steal from anyone. That's it.

308
26:08.510 --> 26:10.913
Okay, talk to you later.

309
26:13.160 --> 26:15.273
Take me to your dad.

310
26:31.070 --> 26:32.310
Well...

311
26:32.310 --> 26:33.630
​Who are these people?

312
26:33.630 --> 26:35.590
​Where did you get this jacket?

313
26:39.177 --> 26:40.880
​Why do you want to know?

314
26:40.880 --> 26:43.040
​I won't beat around the bush.

315
26:43.040 --> 26:47.920
This is my friend's jacket, but he died a few days ago.

316
26:48.800 --> 26:52.933
I want to know how it ended up with you.

317
26:58.711 --> 27:01.355
​Well, I took it from...

318
27:01.355 --> 27:03.340
From the dead man's car, right?

319
27:04.755 --> 27:06.390
​Just answer me.

320
27:09.410 --> 27:12.370
​Dad, just tell them where you got this jacket.

321
27:12.370 --> 27:13.960
​They won't report you to the police.

322
27:13.960 --> 27:16.400
​You really won't report him, right?

323
27:20.270 --> 27:23.880
​If you tell me everything, I won't report you.

324
27:23.880 --> 27:27.320
You do know theft can get you sent to prison, right?

325
27:34.030 --> 27:35.600
​I didn't know he was dead.

326
27:35.600 --> 27:38.190
​I thought he was just sleeping.

327
27:44.980 --> 27:46.420
​So...

328
27:47.750 --> 27:49.940
You really did go to that car.

329
27:51.230 --> 27:55.288
​Damn it, a security guard's salary isn't enough to live on.

330
27:55.288 --> 27:58.410
​I just do some petty theft here and there.

331
27:59.630 --> 28:01.740
I really need the money.

332
28:02.400 --> 28:04.120
​And I'm not hurting anyone.

333
28:04.120 --> 28:07.680
I just steal stuff, and it's not like I do it every day.

334
28:07.680 --> 28:09.860
You don't have to make excuses.

335
28:10.680 --> 28:12.480
​I want to know about this.

336
28:13.290 --> 28:17.000
​What did you see when you went to that car? ​Tell me everything.

337
28:19.330 --> 28:22.570
​Well, I saw a car that had been parked there for a while.

338
28:24.977 --> 28:25.770
Sir.

339
28:25.770 --> 28:28.940
​So I tried opening the door, hoping it wasn't locked.

340
28:29.760 --> 28:33.440
But when it opened, I was shocked to see someone sleeping inside.

341
28:33.440 --> 28:36.050
​Was he dead at that time?

342
28:36.050 --> 28:39.840
I wouldn't know. I just knew he was sleeping.

343
28:39.840 --> 28:43.800
So I just grabbed some valuables and got out of there.

344
28:43.800 --> 28:45.659
​What did you take?

345
28:48.920 --> 28:54.400
The cash in the bag and this jacket.

346
28:54.400 --> 28:57.813
What about the phone and the laptop? Did you take them?

347
28:59.770 --> 29:03.646
Yeah, the phone and the laptop, too.

348
29:07.640 --> 29:09.280
Where are they now?

349
29:10.860 --> 29:12.970
I've already sold them.

350
29:17.977 --> 29:20.560
​Why were you in such a hurry to sell them?

351
29:20.560 --> 29:25.530
Come on, they were stolen. I had to get rid of them as fast as possible.

352
29:25.530 --> 29:29.870
My daughter took this jacket with her, so it's the only thing left.

353
29:29.870 --> 29:32.640
​As for the rest, I've sold them all.

354
29:32.640 --> 29:37.155
​The phone and laptop are probably at the border by now.

355
29:37.155 --> 29:38.973
​You won't be able to track them down.

356
29:49.037 --> 29:54.037
Dad, who did you sell the dead man's phone and laptop to?

357
29:54.920 --> 29:59.253
Maybe they can buy them back. ​It seems they're looking for something.

358
30:04.050 --> 30:06.210
​I can't tell you.

359
30:06.210 --> 30:10.755
​Those things are with someone we should stay far away from.

360
30:28.440 --> 30:29.960
Hey.

361
30:31.640 --> 30:34.280
​Why does everyone always try to startle me?

362
30:35.370 --> 30:37.955
​You're such a scaredy-cat.

363
30:37.955 --> 30:39.426
​What were you thinking about?

364
30:42.160 --> 30:46.840
How are we going to find Anda's phone and laptop?

365
30:47.955 --> 30:49.600
​There might be a way.

366
30:49.600 --> 30:51.200
Let me think about it first.

367
30:51.200 --> 30:53.355
​I'm so exhausted right now.

368
31:02.066 --> 31:03.266
Eat up.

369
31:03.266 --> 31:04.930
This one is good.

370
31:07.640 --> 31:08.860
Eat, come on.

371
31:08.860 --> 31:11.440
Yeah, I'm literally chewing.

372
31:15.120 --> 31:16.950
Have some more.

373
31:17.960 --> 31:22.313
By the way, what's the occasion for this treat?

374
31:23.370 --> 31:25.530
Nothing, really.

375
31:25.530 --> 31:28.120
We've been going through a lot lately,

376
31:28.120 --> 31:31.900
so I thought we could enjoy some food and take a break from all the stress.

377
31:42.640 --> 31:43.920
What?

378
31:45.280 --> 31:48.320
Do I look like someone who only talks about depressing stuff?

379
31:48.320 --> 31:50.640
Exactly. You just realized?

380
31:52.000 --> 31:55.760
You look so unfriendly.

381
31:56.355 --> 31:59.310
That's why I've hated your guts all this time.

382
32:03.920 --> 32:05.720
Be careful.

383
32:05.720 --> 32:08.720
You might end up with what you hate.

384
32:15.840 --> 32:18.560
Sir, please buy some cupcakes.

385
32:20.080 --> 32:23.800
Do you know what time it is? You should go home.

386
32:23.800 --> 32:27.240
I haven't sold them all yet, so I can't go home.

387
32:29.640 --> 32:32.080
Did your parents make you do this?

388
32:32.950 --> 32:35.260
Jinna, don't be so harsh on him.

389
32:37.940 --> 32:43.030
No, sir. My dad is sick and can barely walk. My mom passed away a long time ago.

390
32:48.720 --> 32:50.300
Who do you live with?

391
32:51.200 --> 32:53.100
With my dad and my younger sister.

392
32:53.100 --> 32:56.980
My dad makes these cupcakes. My mom taught him the recipe.

393
33:01.200 --> 33:02.800
Have you eaten yet?

394
33:02.800 --> 33:04.400
Not yet, sir.

395
33:07.960 --> 33:10.760
Eat something first, then I'll buy your cupcakes.

396
33:10.760 --> 33:14.040
I can't stay long, sir. I need to sell all the cupcakes.

397
33:15.133 --> 33:18.533
I'll buy them all, but you should eat first.

398
33:22.850 --> 33:25.230
Eat with us.

399
33:25.230 --> 33:27.110
You'll be home in no time.

400
33:28.466 --> 33:30.440
My friend eats a lot.

401
33:30.440 --> 33:33.000
He'll buy all your cupcakes himself.

402
33:34.400 --> 33:38.880
Can I wrap up the food and take it home instead?

403
33:39.473 --> 33:41.665
Hey, just eat it here.

404
33:41.665 --> 33:43.520
Why do you want to take it home?

405
33:44.720 --> 33:47.440
I want to take it home for my dad and sister.

406
33:59.240 --> 34:04.400
Sir, I'd like one of everything on this table to go.

407
34:09.520 --> 34:11.200
Are you happy now?

408
34:12.930 --> 34:14.810
Can you eat with us now?

409
34:15.680 --> 34:19.940
Thank you, handsome. I hope only good things come your way.

410
34:21.950 --> 34:23.660
"Handsome."

411
34:25.311 --> 34:26.822
Come here.

412
34:31.630 --> 34:33.350
Here you go.

413
34:34.020 --> 34:36.422
Can you eat this? Let me do it for you.

414
34:36.422 --> 34:38.066
How much of this do you want?

415
34:55.340 --> 34:57.340
Get him a glass.

416
34:58.711 --> 35:01.020
I forgot. My bad.

417
35:08.866 --> 35:10.733
Isn't he scary?

418
35:27.911 --> 35:29.640
Hey, Jinna.

419
35:29.640 --> 35:33.060
Why did you have to help that kid so much?

420
35:33.060 --> 35:36.733
Couldn't you just buy some of his cupcakes and leave it at that?

421
35:38.070 --> 35:42.240
I used to have nothing. He reminds me of myself.

422
35:42.240 --> 35:43.560
Why?

423
35:43.560 --> 35:46.555
Is it so strange when I do something good?

424
35:46.555 --> 35:50.240
Hey, I was just asking. Why so prickly?

425
35:50.888 --> 35:53.060
I was actually complimenting you.

426
35:55.100 --> 35:56.980
No need for that.

427
35:57.777 --> 36:00.100
You deserve a reward when you do something good.

428
36:00.670 --> 36:03.950
Do you want anything? I'll get it for you.

429
36:03.950 --> 36:05.240
I can buy it myself.

430
36:05.240 --> 36:06.800
No need to get me anything.

431
36:06.800 --> 36:09.560
There's nothing I want right now.

432
36:09.560 --> 36:13.920
But I'm sure there's something that you really want

433
36:13.920 --> 36:15.960
but money can't buy.

434
36:29.200 --> 36:30.688
Hurry.

435
36:52.830 --> 36:56.780
Hey, I'm soaked. It's all over me.

436
36:56.780 --> 36:58.920
You look like a drowned rat.

437
37:00.666 --> 37:03.970
So, what were you going to give me just now?

438
37:07.330 --> 37:08.900
You're not getting it.

439
37:08.900 --> 37:10.820
You said you didn't want it.

440
37:12.400 --> 37:16.080
So, you're really not giving it to me?

441
37:25.760 --> 37:29.880
Actually, there's something I want but haven't gotten yet.

442
37:33.600 --> 37:37.080
And do you still want it?

443
37:38.950 --> 37:40.460
I do.

444
37:45.560 --> 37:50.720
Do you know which bus lines go past my condo?

445
37:55.330 --> 37:58.180
Line 084.

446
38:03.290 --> 38:05.790
Line 156.

447
38:07.020 --> 38:09.500
Are you sure those are bus lines?

448
38:12.720 --> 38:14.560
Line 44.

449
38:16.711 --> 38:19.430
- Hold on. - And then 65.

450
38:24.900 --> 38:28.420
084... 156, right?

451
38:31.360 --> 38:33.340
084156...

452
38:33.340 --> 38:35.660
What was it again?

453
38:35.660 --> 38:37.640
44, right?

454
38:37.640 --> 38:39.280
44 and...

455
38:40.990 --> 38:43.440
5 and what?

456
38:43.440 --> 38:46.680
- 5... - Jeez, you don't remember?

457
38:52.888 --> 38:55.422
65...

458
38:56.222 --> 38:58.030
Not 56.

459
39:00.590 --> 39:05.190
So, can I call you?

460
39:05.190 --> 39:07.650
Don't you call me all the time anyway?

461
39:07.650 --> 39:11.460
Come on, calling the number is way more classic.

462
39:16.740 --> 39:18.600
Do whatever you want.

463
39:25.880 --> 39:28.200
So I can do whatever I want?

464
39:30.680 --> 39:32.320
Yeah.

465
39:34.300 --> 39:36.990
Have I ever tried to stop you?

466
40:04.720 --> 40:06.280
There are people around.

467
41:46.610 --> 41:49.710
Let's go grab a bite. I'm sick of studying.

468
41:49.710 --> 41:53.500
Bum is focusing on her studies. Let's not go yet.

469
41:54.740 --> 41:56.980
Are you aiming for an A or what?

470
41:56.980 --> 42:01.644
Even if you don't get honors, I'll still love you anyway.

471
42:08.311 --> 42:10.440
I don't think that's what she's aiming for, Podduang.

472
42:10.440 --> 42:12.620
She's just reading Anda's news.

473
42:15.410 --> 42:17.560
Why the annoyed look again?

474
42:17.560 --> 42:19.760
I'm sick of those people on the internet.

475
42:19.760 --> 42:23.360
Anda is already dead, yet they won't stop trash-talking him.

476
42:23.360 --> 42:26.130
Those reporters who interviewed his mom, too.

477
42:26.130 --> 42:27.980
They have zero ethics.

478
42:27.980 --> 42:30.720
Anda just died, and they asked how she felt.

479
42:30.720 --> 42:32.760
Were they expecting her to be happy?

480
42:35.386 --> 42:38.970
I think we need to get to the bottom of this.

481
42:38.970 --> 42:43.520
Maybe it'll make those people see things from Anda's side.

482
42:43.520 --> 42:44.955
Right.

483
42:44.955 --> 42:48.933
So, how much have you and Jinna's friends found out so far?

484
42:48.933 --> 42:52.880
We're taking a break to study for exams.

485
42:52.880 --> 42:55.760
As for Jinna, I don't know how far he's gotten

486
42:55.760 --> 42:58.450
with tracking down Anda's phone and laptop.

487
42:58.450 --> 43:01.680
Why are you so desperate to find his phone and laptop?

488
43:01.680 --> 43:05.000
Jinna said it was suspicious that those two things went missing.

489
43:05.000 --> 43:09.480
We asked the security guard, but he wouldn't tell us who he sold them to.

490
43:09.480 --> 43:14.120
Speaking of which, I'd better call Jinna.

491
43:20.530 --> 43:22.860
He's calling Jinna?

492
43:25.866 --> 43:27.710
What are you guys smiling at?

493
43:28.320 --> 43:29.440
Nothing.

494
43:29.440 --> 43:31.410
Nothing. Go ahead.

495
43:31.410 --> 43:33.720
Call whoever you want.

496
43:33.720 --> 43:35.180
What's wrong with you guys?

497
43:35.180 --> 43:37.050
Take your time. Off you go.

498
43:37.050 --> 43:38.666
Why are you smiling?

499
43:38.666 --> 43:40.666
Your cheeks are turning red.

500
43:42.333 --> 43:44.000
Hello, darling?

501
43:44.000 --> 43:45.660
I kinda ship them.

502
43:45.660 --> 43:47.210
Hey, Podduang.

503
43:47.210 --> 43:49.130
I was just about to call you.

504
43:49.130 --> 43:53.977
I'm sending Art and Tod after the laptop and phone at malls and thrift stores.

505
43:54.644 --> 43:56.380
At thrift stores?

506
43:56.380 --> 43:59.420
Yeah, I'm having them check thrift stores first

507
43:59.420 --> 44:02.311
since the security guard gave us no lead on where he sold them.

508
44:02.311 --> 44:04.511
I see.

509
44:04.511 --> 44:10.088
So do you think you'll find anything on Anda's laptop and phone?

510
44:10.088 --> 44:13.360
I don't know, but I think they're the easiest places to start.

511
44:13.360 --> 44:16.644
At least we'll know who he was talking to before he died.

512
44:16.644 --> 44:18.066
Okay.

513
44:18.870 --> 44:21.460
Have you eaten yet?

514
44:21.460 --> 44:23.040
Not yet.

515
44:23.710 --> 44:26.310
I'm studying with my friends.

516
44:26.310 --> 44:27.660
Go get some food.

517
44:27.660 --> 44:29.886
Why are you studying so hard?

518
44:31.360 --> 44:36.480
If I don't study, how will I pass my exams? Are you out of your mind?

519
44:38.400 --> 44:40.080
I miss you.

520
44:43.270 --> 44:48.088
We were talking about something serious, and now you're suddenly saying you miss me?

521
44:53.240 --> 44:56.560
Can't I do both? What's so strange about that?

522
44:59.088 --> 45:01.800
Jeez. Bye.

523
45:01.800 --> 45:04.900
Just go practice. You talk too much.

524
45:04.900 --> 45:07.180
Come back soon. I miss you.

525
45:08.080 --> 45:09.680
Bye for now.

526
45:17.622 --> 45:21.160
Risa, what are you doing here? You startled me.

527
45:21.160 --> 45:24.760
I thought you didn't like him. You were blushing like crazy.

528
45:24.760 --> 45:29.240
I wasn't. I'm just tired. My back hurts.

529
45:29.240 --> 45:31.795
I need to talk to you about something.

530
45:33.560 --> 45:35.680
About what?

531
45:35.680 --> 45:37.080
About Jinna.

532
45:37.080 --> 45:40.320
I don't care whether or not you like Jinna.

533
45:40.320 --> 45:44.200
If you like him, that's fine. But I like him, too.

534
45:45.320 --> 45:50.120
He doesn't belong to anyone yet, so let's compete to win him over.

535
45:51.440 --> 45:52.693
Deal?

536
45:56.520 --> 45:57.670
That's it. I'm off.

537
45:57.670 --> 46:00.800
Risa, we're not finished talking yet...

538
46:00.800 --> 46:02.950
Where are you going?

539
46:02.950 --> 46:04.660
To find Jinna.

540
46:10.770 --> 46:12.370
You should go, too.

541
46:15.480 --> 46:17.000
Follow her.

542
46:18.000 --> 46:20.840
- Hurry! - Hurry up, Podduang!

543
46:22.280 --> 46:23.410
I'm still in shock.

544
46:23.410 --> 46:25.520
- What are you waiting for? Go! - Just go!

545
46:27.200 --> 46:29.320
Do you still have practice today?

546
46:29.320 --> 46:31.153
Whatever you think has nothing to do with me.

547
46:31.153 --> 46:33.120
We're just pretending to flirt, remember?

548
46:33.120 --> 46:35.180
It's not like we're actually flirting.

549
46:35.180 --> 46:37.820
What else did you take from Anda's car besides the jacket?

550
46:37.820 --> 46:39.380
These earbuds, too?

551
46:40.033 --> 46:41.550
You haven't slept with Jinna yet, have you?

552
46:41.550 --> 46:43.510
What kind of question is that?

553
46:44.100 --> 46:47.180
I know you're stressing over what happened to Anda,

554
46:48.210 --> 46:53.488
but I promise that no matter what happens, I'll always be here for you.
